{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793474249,"nonce":"XTNumqgW16G0Rh+yEuGYAWq7LWg=","message":"First part landed: native/sync gateway module (SyncWorkspace). Pure state for one synced workspace, no I/O: begin reserves quota for the chunks the workspace does not hold (workspace allocation and account total, in-flight reservations counted), record_chunk is idempotent and size-checked, pending lists what is left after a dropped connection, publish verifies and validates the manifest, checks the compare and swap against the base generation, requires every declared chunk to be received and durable (the caller supplies durable), turns the reservation into referenced bytes, starts the expiry clock only on the first publication and reports garbage; cancel, sweep (lease 60 min, at most 4 uploads) and revoke return reservations and void leases. 19 unit tests cover dedup, forged and mismatched chunks, forged manifest, undeclared chunk, stale base generation, concurrent quota exhaustion, account quota, expired and revoked leases, expiry clock, and storing and loading the state. Not done: the Worker side in web/cloud (Durable Object holding SyncWorkspace in SQLite storage, R2 chunk streaming with length and hash checks, routes under the account, alarm for the sweep, export), the miniflare tests the issue lists (oversized manifest, forged checksum over the wire, DO restart between upload and publish, resume after a dropped connection), and the account directory and sign-in dependency (92e2f4e): routes can use the existing GitHub session cookie meanwhile.","files":null}]}